Upstream-Name: Climat
Upstream-Contact: https://github.com/JowiAoun/climat/issues
Source: https://github.com/JowiAoun/climat
Comment:
 Installed as /usr/share/doc/climat/copyright, and it is not a formality: the
 climat binary is statically linked and carries a typeface, a place-name
 database and several recorded weather-service payloads inside it. Every one of
 those arrives under somebody else's licence, and a copyright file that named
 only the GPL would be describing a package that is not this one.
 .
 The authoritative, per-file record is the SPDX metadata in the source tree -
 every file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier header, and REUSE.toml covers
 the binaries and the JSON that cannot. `reuse lint` over the source is what
 keeps this file honest. What follows is that record collapsed to the grouping
 Debian asks for.

Files: *
Copyright: 2026 Jowi Aoun
License: GPL-3.0-or-later

Files: libclimat/*
Copyright: 2026 Jowi Aoun
License: MPL-2.0
Comment:
 The engine is deliberately weaker-copyleft than the application it serves, so
 that it stays reusable outside a GPL program - decision D6 in
 docs/03-tech-stack.md. It links no Qt GUI module and a CMake assertion
 enforces that.

Files: packaging/icons/*
 docs/*
 README.md
Copyright: 2026 Jowi Aoun
License: CC-BY-SA-4.0
Comment: Artwork and prose rather than code, per D6.

Files: app/fonts/Inter-Regular.ttf
 app/fonts/Inter-Bold.ttf
Copyright: 2016 The Inter Project Authors (https://github.com/rsms/inter)
License: OFL-1.1
Comment:
 Compiled into the binary and installed with it. Both files carry the copyright
 in name ID 0 and the licence in name ID 13 of their own name tables, which is
 how OFL section 2 asks a binary redistribution to carry the notice; we do not
 strip them.

Files: libclimat/providers/geocoding/data/cities15000.cgx
Copyright: GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org)
License: CC-BY-4.0
Comment:
 The offline reverse-geocoding index, compiled into the binary. It is the
 GeoNames cities15000 dump reduced to seven columns and deflated; trimming
 columns and changing the container does not make it ours. The credit CC-BY
 requires is shown at run time under About, Data sources.

Files: libclimat/providers/fixture/data/*/forecast.json
 libclimat/providers/fixture/data/*/airquality.json
Copyright: Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com)
License: CC-BY-4.0
Comment:
 Recorded API responses, compiled into the binary so that --fixture renders
 without a network. Credited at run time under About, Data sources.

Files: libclimat/providers/fixture/data/toronto/alerts.json
